#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fort Galgs: a front end for fortctl's CPU reservation.

This is a front end. Every change to the machine belongs to fortctl, which
this program shells out to; if a change fails, its own words are what the
user sees. The live picture reads /proc/stat and cgroup cpu.stat directly,
because those are read-only and cheap.

Run with --self-test to build every page and draw every state once, or with
--snapshot <png> to draw the chip from live load.
"""

